#import "/modern-iaf/manuals/text/en/f16/ch1/src.typ": *

Before the first switch of the checklist card, the pilot of the real jet checks the aircraft from the outside and the cockpit from the ladder. The sim has none of this: it is #term("not modelled"), and the jet stands ready with its canopy open. This section gives the real order in outline, so that the card's first section (@cold-start) is seen in its place.

=== The forms and the walk-around <preflight-exterior>

+ *The aircraft's forms.* The pilot reads the jet's maintenance forms: that the jet is released for flight, and which stores it carries#fm[section II, "Preflight check", page 2-2].
+ *The exterior inspection.* The pilot walks around the jet along a fixed route and looks at each part of it on the way#fm[section II, "Exterior inspection", page 2-2, which refers to the manual's figure 2-4, page 2-33, for the route]. What is checked at each stop is in the figure, which this manual does not repeat. Inferred, as on any jet: no leaks, no damage, the covers and safety pins removed, the stores as the forms say.

=== Cockpit entry <preflight-entry>

+ *The canopy* is opened from the outside, with a switch under the left strake#fm[section II, "Cockpit access", page 2-2 and its figure 2-1].
+ *The ladder* goes on the cockpit sill only after the canopy has stopped moving: a canopy whose actuator fails can fall on its way up#fm[section II, "Cockpit access", item 2, page 2-2].
+ *The ejection seat* is checked before the pilot sits in it: the ejection safety lever up (safe), the two safety pins removed, the seat's straps, hoses and emergency oxygen bottle in order#fm[section II, "Before entering cockpit", item 1, page 2-2].
+ *The cockpit interior check* follows, seated: a pass over the left console, the front panel and the right console that puts every switch in its position for the start#fm[section II, "Cockpit interior check", from page 2-3]. The card's first section, "Before starting engine", holds the items of that pass that matter in the sim.

#idx("Wind, canopy")#caution[In a wind above 30 kt the real canopy is opened only as far as needed to climb in or out: a smaller opening angle lowers the chance that the wind blows the canopy past its full-open stop#fm[section II, "Cockpit access", item 1, page 2-2]. The sim's wind does not move the canopy.]

#in-sim[The jet stands parked, checked and with the canopy open. #sym.arrow.r *Nothing to do*: go on with @cold-start. Not modelled: the forms, the walk-around, the ladder, the seat's check.]
